4. the following algorithm training pipleine should be implemented.
  Algorithm Training Pipeline (What Should Exist)

  Current Algorithms

  1. Avellaneda-Stoikov (Classic)
     - No training needed
     - Parameter optimization via grid search
     - Inputs: spread_bps, skew, entropy_threshold

  2. ML Spread/Skew (Linear)
     - Training: walk-forward-ml command
     - Learns: entropy→spread, volatility→spread, inventory→skew
     - Weights stored in presets

  Algorithms to Add (Roadmap)

  3. Gradient Boosted Trees (XGBoost/LightGBM)
     - Train on: features → optimal_spread, optimal_skew
     - Better non-linear relationships
     - Requires: Python integration or Rust ML crate

  4. Neural Network Policy
     - Train on: state → action (quote placement)
     - Can learn complex patterns
     - Requires: PyTorch/TensorFlow bridge

  5. Reinforcement Learning (PPO/SAC)
     - Train via simulation episodes
     - Reward: realized P&L - risk penalty
     - State: features + inventory + recent trades
     - Action: spread, skew, quote/no-quote
     - Requires: RL framework integration

  6. Ensemble/Meta-Learner
     - Combines predictions from multiple algorithms
     - Learns which algorithm works in which regime
     - Requires: all base algorithms implemented


